  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# ML Pipelines Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The code in `code/pipeline.py` builds a complete ML pipeline from scratch:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Custom Transformer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class CustomTransformer:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.means = None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.stds = None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def fit(self, X):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.means = np.mean(X, axis=0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.stds = np.std(X, axis=0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.stds[self.stds == 0] = 1.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def transform(self, X):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return (X - self.means) / self.stds"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def fit_transform(self, X):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self.fit(X).transform(X)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Pipeline from Scratch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class PipelineFromScratch:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, steps):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.steps = steps"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def fit(self, X, y=None):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        X_current = X.copy()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for name, step in self.steps[:-1]:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            X_current = step.fit_transform(X_current)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        name, model = self.steps[-1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        model.fit(X_current, y)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def predict(self, X):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        X_current = X.copy()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for name, step in self.steps[:-1]:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            X_current = step.transform(X_current)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        name, model = self.steps[-1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return model.predict(X_current)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Cross-Validation with Pipeline"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The code demonstrates how cross-validation with a pipeline prevents data leakage: the scaler is fit separately on each fold's training data."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Full Production Pipeline with sklearn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "A complete pipeline with `ColumnTransformer`, multiple preprocessing paths, and a model, trained with proper cross-validation and experiment logging."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Build a pipeline that handles a dataset with 3 numeric columns and 2 categorical columns. Use `ColumnTransformer` to apply median imputation + scaling to numerics and most-frequent imputation + one-hot encoding to categoricals. Train with 5-fold cross-validation.\n\n2. Deliberately introduce data leakage: fit the scaler on the full dataset before splitting. Compare the cross-validation score (leaky) to the pipeline cross-validation score (clean). How large is the difference?\n\n3. Serialize your pipeline with `joblib.dump`. Load it in a separate script and run predictions. Verify the predictions are identical.\n\n4. Add a custom transformer to the pipeline that creates polynomial features (degree 2) for the two most important numeric columns. Where should it go in the pipeline?\n\n5. Set up MLflow tracking for the pipeline. Run 5 experiments with different hyperparameters. Use the MLflow UI (`mlflow ui`) to compare runs and pick the best model."
      ]
    }
